course: dictionary
lesson: 4335
title: Meeting a creature from context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name creatures you cannot find in a zoo or a garden. Context helps here, because the words around the word describe it for you. «A Gryphon (also spelled griffin) is a creature from old stories, half eagle and half lion» tells you what it looks like, even if you have never heard of one.
explain: Spellings can change too. Gryphon, griffin and griffon are different spellings of the same word. When you meet a new spelling, check the sentence for a clue such as «also spelled», or ask whether the writer is talking about a creature you already know by another name.
explain: Some words also name a character in a story. In Alice in Wonderland, the Gryphon is one of the characters who meets Alice, so it is a name for a creature in one book as well as a creature from old tales. Read the whole paragraph to see which meaning the writer means.
fact: Gryphon means a made-up creature from old stories.
fact: A gryphon has the head, wings and front legs of an eagle, and the body, back legs and tail of a lion.
fact: Gryphon can also be spelled griffin or griffon.
fact: Gryphons are shown on coats of arms, flags and old buildings, where they stand for strength and watchfulness.
fact: No gryphon ever lived, so it is not a real animal.
exercise: «A Gryphon (also spelled griffin) is a creature from old stories, half eagle and half lion.» What is a gryphon? | *A made-up creature from old stories, half eagle and half lion | A kind of soup from the sea | A type of fish with a long tail | A real animal found in zoos
exercise: The sentence above gives another spelling of gryphon. Find and copy it. | lobster | *griffin | eagle | Mock Turtle
exercise: Is a gryphon a real animal? | Yes, it lives in Persia today | Yes, it lives in zoos | Yes, it lives in the sea | *No, it is made up and no gryphon ever lived
test: «The Queen wakes a Gryphon sleeping in the sun and orders it to take Alice to the Mock Turtle.» Which animal parts make up a gryphon? | Fish tail and eagle wings | Dog head and tail; bird wings | Lion head, wings and front legs; eagle body and tail | *Eagle head, wings and front legs; lion body, back legs and tail
test: In Alice in Wonderland, what does the Gryphon do with Alice? | *Takes her to meet the Mock Turtle | Gives her a golden crown | Takes her home | Carries her across the sea
exam: Gryphons are often drawn on coats of arms and old buildings. What do they stand for there? | *Strength and watchfulness | Lost treasure and old maps | Plain fun and games | Rain and cold winds
